 **P-257. MCP auth headers and client-credentials renewal.** Phase 9 review (correctness 7, 8). With `auth` or `auth_provider`, a user `Authorization` header went out next to the bearer token (`reqwest` appends); and a client-credentials token was granted once per connection, so after expiry `rmcp`'s refresh (client-credentials responses carry no refresh token) failed and requests went out unauthenticated until `connect(true)`. TS sets the token with `headers.set("Authorization", ..)`, and its non-interactive provider runs the grant again on a 401. Choice: with `auth` or `auth_provider`, `authorization` is dropped from the custom headers, so the token wins. The url-configured client with `auth` uses a private `StreamableHttpClient` (`mcp::auth::ClientCredentialsClient`) around the granted `AuthClient`: before each request it takes the stored token, or runs the grant again when `rmcp` reports none usable; on a 401 it runs the grant again (once per rejected grant, shared by concurrent requests) and retries once. A freshly granted token is used as granted, without `rmcp`'s 30-second expiry margin, so a server issuing tokens shorter than 30 s still works. TS reference: `@modelcontextprotocol/client` `dist/index.mjs:5444-5452,5740-5752`. Files: `src/mcp/auth.rs`, `src/mcp/client.rs`.
 
 **P-258. MCP prompt and resource lists without the capability; P-258 amends P-248.** Phase 9 review (correctness 9). Only `list_tools` checked the server capability; `list_prompts`, `list_resources` and `list_resource_templates` sent the request and failed with `-32601` against a tools-only server. The MCP SDK returns `{ prompts: [] }` / `{ resources: [] }` / `{ resourceTemplates: [] }` when the capability is missing. Choice: each list method returns the empty (`Default`) result when the connected server lacks `prompts` (prompts) or `resources` (resources and templates). TS reference: `@modelcontextprotocol/client` `dist/index.mjs:3681-3684,3719-3722`. Files: `src/mcp/client.rs`.
+
+**P-259. Phase 9 public surface fixes; P-259 amends P-217, P-231, P-235, P-248 and P-250.** Phase 9 review (API 1-8). (1) `regex` (`McpToolMatcher::Pattern`, `From<Regex>`) and `reqwest` (`McpAuthProvider = AuthClient<reqwest::Client>`) are public dependencies of the `mcp` feature, so `strands::mcp::regex` and `strands::mcp::reqwest` re-export them, as P-217 does for the AWS crates and `http` (amends P-217 and P-231). (2) `McpServerCredentials` is gone: `McpClientCredentials` (TS has one type, `config.ts:38`) derives `Serialize`/`Deserialize` (camelCase, `scopes` omitted when `None`) and keeps its redacting `Debug`, and `McpServerConfig::auth` is `Option<McpClientCredentials>` (amends P-250). (3) `McpClientCredentials`, `McpToolFilters`, `SerializableMcpToolFilters`, `McpServerConfig` and `McpLoadServersOptions` derive `bon::Builder` (#65). (4) `McpServerConfig::tasks_config` is removed: the raw entry's `tasksConfig` is rejected before parsing with the same text (`MCP tasks ("tasksConfig") are not supported in Rust yet`), so a typed `TasksConfig` can be added later without a breaking change. (5) `list_prompts()`, `list_resources()` and `list_resource_templates()` take no arguments, with `list_prompts_with`, `list_resources_with` and `list_resource_templates_with(McpListOptions)` for one page, matching `list_tools`/`list_tools_with` and TS's optional `options` (amends P-248). (6) `connect_with(reconnect, McpConnectOptions)`, where `McpConnectOptions { cancel_signal: Option<CancelSignal> }` is a config struct with `Default` and a builder (TS `connect(reconnect, options?: { signal })`; amends P-235). (7) Accessors TS lacks, kept as small idiomatic accessors: `McpClient::client_version()` (the handshake version beside TS's `clientName`), `McpClient::negotiated_protocol_version()` (TS reaches it as `client.getNegotiatedProtocolVersion()` through the SDK client; here it saves going through `peer()`), and `McpTool::server_name()` (TS keeps the server-side name in a private `WeakMap`; Rust callers need it for filters and `call_tool` diagnostics). (8) Erratum for the lead: P-233's cross-reference "`McpTransport::sse(..)` (P-238)" should read P-241. Files: `src/mcp/{mod,client,config,filters}.rs`.
